    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nO' Donnellan & Joyce Auctioneers are delighted to offer a rare opportunity to acquire approximately 44 acres of coastal land at Lehanagh South, Cashel, Co. Galway.\n\nSet along the shores of Cashel Bay, this unique holding enjoys an exceptional combination of natural beauty, privacy and traditional character. The property is approached via an old stone track from the public road and extends towards the shoreline, with the land offering a mixture of meadow, grazing and rugged coastal landscape.\n\nAt the heart of the property are the ruins of a traditional stone cottage, together with a number of adjoining stone outbuildings. These attractive historic structures provide a striking focal point and could offer significant potential for restoration or redevelopment, subject to the necessary planning permissions. \n\nApproximately 32 acres are held in private ownership, with a further 12 acres of commonage, and the land benefits from good natural boundaries and extensive frontage towards the bay. The surrounding landscape is characterised by mature vegetation, stone walls, rocky outcrops and open coastal views.\n\nThe setting is particularly special, combining peace and seclusion with spectacular views across Cashel Bay and the surrounding Connemara countryside. The property is situated approximately 5 miles from Recess, 16 miles from Clifden and 40 miles from Galway City.\n\n\nKeep up to-date with NEW PROPERTIES by registering your details on our database For Further details please contact our office on 091-564212 OFFICE OPENING HOURS - MON TO FRI 9AM TO 5:30PMProperties can be viewed on our website www.odj.ie NOTE: These particulars are not to be considered a formal offer. They are for information only and give a general idea of the property. They are not to be taken as forming any part of a resulting contract, nor to be relied upon as statements or representations of fact. Whilst every care is taken in their preparation, neither O'Donnellan & Joyce Auctioneers nor the vendor accept any liability as to their accuracy. Intending purchasers must satisfy themselves by personal inspection or otherwise as to the correctness of these particulars. No person in the employment of O'Donnellan & Joyce Auctioneers has any authority to make or give any representation or warranty whatever in relation to this property."
      },
